{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nThere are a lot of things which could be cut\u00a0\u2014 trees, paper, \"the rope\". In this problem you are going to cut a sequence of integers.There is a sequence of integers, which contains the equal number of even and odd numbers. Given a limited budget, you need to make maximum possible number of cuts such that each resulting segment will have the same number of odd and even integers.Cuts separate a sequence to continuous (contiguous) segments. You may think about each cut as a break between two adjacent elements in a sequence. So after cutting each element belongs to exactly one segment. Say, $$$[4, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 4, 4, 5, 5]$$$ $$$\\to$$$ two cuts $$$\\to$$$ $$$[4, 1 | 2, 3, 4, 5 | 4, 4, 5, 5]$$$. On each segment the number of even elements should be equal to the number of odd elements.The cost of the cut between $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$ numbers is $$$|x - y|$$$ bitcoins. Find the maximum possible number of cuts that can be made while spending no more than $$$B$$$ bitcoins.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.math.*;\nimport java.lang.*;\n\nimport static java.lang.Math.*;\n\npublic class Main implements Runnable {\n    static class Tokenizer {\n        private BufferedReader reader;\n        private String currentLine;\n        private String[] tokens;\n        private int index;\n\n        public Tokenizer() {\n            reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n            index = 0;\n        }\n\n        private void loadLine() {\n            try {\n                currentLine = reader.readLine();\n                if (currentLine != null) {\n                    tokens = currentLine.trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n                    index = 0;\n                }\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(e);\n            }\n        }\n\n        private String next() {\n            if (tokens == null || index >= tokens.length) {\n                loadLine();\n            }\n            return tokens[index++];\n        }\n\n        public int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        public long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        public double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n    }\n\n    static long modPow(long b, long e, long m) {\n        long r = 1;\n        b %= m;\n        while (e > 0) {\n            if ((e & 1) == 1) r = (r * b) % m;\n            b = (b * b) % m;\n            e >>= 1;\n        }\n        return r;\n    }\n\n    static long modInv(long a, long m) {\n        return modPow(a, m - 2, m);\n    }\n\n    static int[][][][] memoTable;\n\n    int traverse(int position, int[] input, int length, int cap, int totalDiff, int oddCount, int selected) {\n        if (position == length) return 0;\n        if (memoTable[position][totalDiff][oddCount][selected] != -1)\n            return memoTable[position][totalDiff][oddCount][selected];\n\n        int take = 0;\n        if (totalDiff + Math.abs(input[position] - input[position - 1]) <= cap && selected - oddCount == oddCount) {\n            take = 1 + traverse(position + 1, input, length, cap,\n                    totalDiff + Math.abs(input[position] - input[position - 1]),\n                    oddCount + (input[position] % 2 == 1 ? 1 : 0), selected + 1);\n        }\n\n        int leave = traverse(position + 1, input, length, cap,\n                totalDiff, oddCount + (input[position] % 2 == 1 ? 1 : 0), selected + 1);\n\n        return memoTable[position][totalDiff][oddCount][selected] = Math.max(take, leave);\n    }\n\n    public void run() {\n        Tokenizer tokenizer = new Tokenizer();\n        PrintWriter writer = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        int n = tokenizer.nextInt();\n        int k = tokenizer.nextInt();\n        int[] data = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            data[i] = tokenizer.nextInt();\n        }\n\n        memoTable = new int[101][101][101][101];\n        for (int i = 0; i < 101; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 101; j++) {\n                for (int l = 0; l < 101; l++) {\n                    Arrays.fill(memoTable[i][j][l], -1);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        int outcome = traverse(1, data, n, k, 0, (data[0] % 2 == 1) ? 1 : 0, 1);\n        writer.println(outcome);\n        writer.close();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        new Thread(null, new Main(), \"Main\", 1 << 26).start();\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.math.*;\nimport java.lang.*;\n\nimport static java.lang.Math.*;\n\npublic class Main implements Runnable {\n    static class Tokenizer {\n        private BufferedReader reader;\n        private String currentLine;\n        private String[] tokens;\n        private int index;\n\n        public Tokenizer() {\n            reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n            index = 0;\n        }\n\n        private void loadLine() {\n            try {\n                currentLine = reader.readLine();\n                if (currentLine != null) {\n                    tokens = currentLine.trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n                    index = 0;\n                }\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(e);\n            }\n        }\n\n        private String next() {\n            if (tokens == null || index >= tokens.length) {\n                loadLine();\n            }\n            return tokens[index++];\n        }\n\n        public int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        public long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        public double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n    }\n\n    public void run() {\n        Tokenizer tokenizer = new Tokenizer();\n        PrintWriter writer = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        int n = tokenizer.nextInt();\n        int budget = tokenizer.nextInt();\n        int[] data = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            data[i] = tokenizer.nextInt();\n        }\n\n        // Find all valid cut positions and their costs\n        List<Integer> cutPositions = new ArrayList<>();\n        List<Integer> cutCosts = new ArrayList<>();\n        \n        int oddCount = 0;\n        int evenCount = 0;\n        \n        // Count total odds and evens to verify they're equal\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (data[i] % 2 == 1) oddCount++;\n            else evenCount++;\n        }\n        \n        // Reset counters for prefix counting\n        oddCount = 0;\n        evenCount = 0;\n        \n        // Find valid cut positions (between elements)\n        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n            if (data[i] % 2 == 1) oddCount++;\n            else evenCount++;\n            \n            // Check if we can make a cut after position i\n            // This means the prefix [0..i] should have equal odd and even counts\n            if (oddCount == evenCount) {\n                int cost = Math.abs(data[i] - data[i + 1]);\n                cutPositions.add(i + 1);\n                cutCosts.add(cost);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Now we want to select maximum number of cuts with total cost <= budget\n        // This is a classic knapsack-like problem: maximize count with cost constraint\n        // Since we want maximum count, we should prefer cheaper cuts\n        \n        // Sort cuts by cost (greedy approach: take cheapest cuts first)\n        int m = cutCosts.size();\n        int[] costs = new int[m];\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n            costs[i] = cutCosts.get(i);\n        }\n        Arrays.sort(costs);\n        \n        int maxCuts = 0;\n        int totalCost = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n            if (totalCost + costs[i] <= budget) {\n                totalCost += costs[i];\n                maxCuts++;\n            } else {\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        writer.println(maxCuts);\n        writer.close();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        new Thread(null, new Main(), \"Main\", 1 << 26).start();\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.152555099310121e-07, -5.9602869441732764e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, -1.7404405298293568e-05, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -5.364403477869928e-06, -8.702239938429557e-06, -1.4662635294371285e-05, -5.960446742392378e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.007674968335777521, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -4.887569048150908e-06, -0.0003871168300975114, -0.00045158201828598976, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.1801649